========================================================================
  [ok]   closed form = squared normalised Dirichlet sum (Fejer-type kernel), primes f < 48, k <= 3f
  [ok]   strictly decreasing on k = 1..f-1, R(f-1,f) = 1/(f-1)^2, R(f,f) = 0
  [ok]   R(uf, f) -> sinc^2(u) as f -> infinity (calculus; standard)
  [ok]   'zero-width gate': for b = pq (p<q), no x < p shares a factor with b, and x = p does (trivial)
